On Wed, 31 Dec 2003, Clive Crous wrote:
> the only pitfall with this patch is that the tty window port draws the
> colour black as "blue" which seems a bit odd at first, but still works
> fine. thanks to Pasi Kallinen for mentioning a possible fix by Jason Short
> changing the tty-blue to dark-gray or "bright-black". this patch can be
> found here :
> http://cs.joensuu.fi/~pkalli/code/color_bright_black.diff

Try my patch at:
ftp://ftp.ocis.net/pub/users/ldeutsch/beta/nethack-3.4.3-gray-1.diff.bz2
instead.

The other patch is much simpler, but relies on reassigning the color
numbers in the non-window-specific game code.  I consider this poor
software design, as it will break or be broken by any other window-system
doing a similar thing.

It is also a permanent change, while my patch installs a new
"use_darkgray" option that must be specifically invoked by the user. So
one doesn't need to worry about stranding users who have terminals with
true bolding (ie: illegible bold-black-on-black).

Also, it's up to date for 3.4.3.

